IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force from 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026): part sga1, module 1.
-- Part 4, Division 2: restrictions on allotment and commencement of business, ss 59 to 62.
-- Part 4 Division 1 (ss 43 to 56) and ss 57, 58 are shown repealed (coverage table in NOTES.md); there is no code for them.
--
-- Every function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN (or another MAYBE) so that JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words
-- and NOTHING is "the text does not say". A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. The rule of 2026-10-29 and the two readings
-- "for a lawyer" are in NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sga1)").
-- Where the text is a bar ("must not ... unless"), the function is named for the bar: JUST TRUE means "barred", JUST FALSE means
-- "the bar does not apply on these facts", and NOTHING means "outside what the bar covers".

§ `Part 4 Division 2: restrictions on allotment and commencement of business`

§§ `Section 59(1): no allotment without a statement in lieu of prospectus lodged at least 3 days before`

-- (1) A public company having a share capital which issued no prospectus on or with reference to its formation must not allot shares or debentures
-- unless a statement in lieu of prospectus complying with the Act was lodged with the Registrar at least 3 days before the first allotment.
-- Scope ("A public company having a share capital which does not issue a prospectus"): a company outside it is not covered (periods ruling (c)): NOTHING.
-- The gate ("unless, at least 3 days before ...") is the text's own: when it is met the bar does not apply (JUST FALSE); when not, the allotment is barred (JUST TRUE).
-- src:6148 | 59.—(1) A public company having a share capital which does not
-- src:6150 | issue a prospectus on or with reference to its formation must not allot
-- src:6151 | any of its shares or debentures unless, at least 3 days before the first
-- src:6152 | allotment of either shares or debentures, there has been lodged with
-- src:6153 | the Registrar a statement in lieu of prospectus which complies with
-- src:6154 | the requirements of this Act.
@ref s 59(1) (src:6148-6154)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company issued a prospectus on or with reference to its formation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement in lieu of prospectus has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the statement in lieu of prospectus was lodged` IS A DATE
      `the day of the first allotment of either shares or debentures` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(1) the company is barred from allotting shares or debentures` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the company is a public company`)
       OR (NOT `the company has a share capital`)
       OR `the company issued a prospectus on or with reference to its formation`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company having a share capital which does not issue a prospectus on or with reference to its formation must not allot" -- a company outside that description is not covered
    ELSE (IF    `a statement in lieu of prospectus has been lodged with the Registrar`
            AND `the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act`
            AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the statement in lieu of prospectus was lodged` `the day of the first allotment of either shares or debentures` 3 Days
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, at least 3 days before the first allotment of either shares or debentures, there has been lodged with the Registrar a statement in lieu of prospectus which complies with the requirements of this Act"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- The same bar as a prohibition on the company (the text names the bearer: N2 ruling of 2026-11-04, SHANT derived from the bar).
DECLARE `s 59 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 59(1) allot shares or debentures without a complying statement in lieu of prospectus lodged at least 3 days before the first allotment`

@ref s 59(1) (src:6148-6154)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 59 act`
`s 59(1) a public company must not allot without a statement in lieu of prospectus` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 59(1) allot shares or debentures without a complying statement in lieu of prospectus lodged at least 3 days before the first allotment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company allotted shares or debentures without a complying statement in lieu of prospectus lodged at least 3 days before the first allotment"

§§ `Section 59(2): the offence of default`

-- (2) If default is made in complying with this section the company and every officer of the company who is in default are guilty of an offence:
-- a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months ("or": the text does not say "or both"; fork F-RS1).
-- src:6156 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section the company
-- src:6157 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:6158 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:6159 | $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months.
@ref s 59(2) (src:6156-6159)
DECLARE `s 59(2) penalty` HAS
    `s 59(2) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 59(2) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 59(2) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 59(2) a default penalty is also payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 59(2) the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
@ref s 59(2) (src:6156-6159)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 59` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `default is made in complying with section 59`
      AND (`the person is the company` OR `the person is an officer of the company who is in default`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If default is made in complying with this section the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence
@ref s 59(2) (src:6156-6159)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 59` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 59(2) penalty`
`s 59(2) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 59(2) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 59` `the person is the company` `the person is an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 59(2) penalty` OF 5000, 12, FALSE, FALSE, 0)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty


§§ `Section 59(3): a director who knowingly contravenes, permits or authorises the contravention`

-- (3) Every director of a company who knowingly contravenes or permits or authorises the contravention of subsection (1) (a) is guilty of an offence; and
-- (b) is liable, in addition to the penalty or punishment, to compensate the company and the allottee respectively for any loss, damages or costs sustained or incurred thereby.
-- The text names no penalty for the offence in (3)(a).
-- src:6164 | (3) Every director of a company who knowingly contravenes or
-- src:6165 | permits or authorises the contravention of subsection (1) shall —
-- src:6167 | (a) be guilty of an offence; and
@ref s 59(3)(a) (src:6164-6167)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly contravened subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly permitted the contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly authorised the contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(3)(a) the director is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director of the company`
      AND (   `the director knowingly contravened subsection (1)`
           OR `the director knowingly permitted the contravention of subsection (1)`
           OR `the director knowingly authorised the contravention of subsection (1)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Every director of a company who knowingly contravenes or permits or authorises the contravention of subsection (1) shall -- (a) be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

-- (3)(a) states no fine and no term: whatever punishment follows is not in these provisions.
@ref s 59(3)(a) (src:6164-6167)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly contravened subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly permitted the contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly authorised the contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 59(3)(a) the highest fine for the offence` MEANS
    NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3)(a) says the director "shall be guilty of an offence" and states no fine and no term; any general penalty is outside the provisions of this part

-- src:6169 | (b) be liable in addition to the penalty or punishment for the
-- src:6170 | offence to compensate the company and allottee
-- src:6171 | respectively for any loss, damages or costs which the
-- src:6172 | company or allottee has sustained or incurred thereby.
@ref s 59(3)(b) (src:6169-6172)
DECLARE `s 59(3)(b) compensation` HAS
    `s 59(3)(b) the amount payable to the company, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 59(3)(b) the amount payable to the allottee, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER

@ref s 59(3)(b) (src:6169-6172)
GIVEN `the person is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly contravened subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly permitted the contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director knowingly authorised the contravention of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss, damages or costs the company has sustained or incurred by the contravention, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the loss, damages or costs the allottee has sustained or incurred by the contravention, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 59(3)(b) compensation`
`s 59(3)(b) what the director is liable to compensate` MEANS
    IF `s 59(3)(a) the director is guilty of an offence` `the person is a director of the company` `the director knowingly contravened subsection (1)` `the director knowingly permitted the contravention of subsection (1)` `the director knowingly authorised the contravention of subsection (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 59(3)(b) compensation` OF `the loss, damages or costs the company has sustained or incurred by the contravention, in Singapore dollars`, `the loss, damages or costs the allottee has sustained or incurred by the contravention, in Singapore dollars`)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection makes liable only a director who knowingly contravenes, permits or authorises the contravention; it says nothing of anyone else

§§ `Section 59(4): two years to sue for the compensation`

-- (4) No proceedings for the compensation in (3)(b) may be commenced after the expiration of 2 years from the date of the allotment.
-- The bar: JUST TRUE once the 2 years have gone; before then the bar does not apply (periods ruling (a): a period fixed in the text's own words).
-- src:6174 | (4) No proceedings for the recovery of any compensation referred
-- src:6175 | to in subsection (3)(b) may be commenced after the expiration of
-- src:6176 | 2 years from the date of the allotment.
@ref s 59(4) (src:6174-6176)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for the recovery of compensation referred to in subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the allotment` IS A DATE
      `the day the proceedings are commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 59(4) the proceedings are barred by the time limit` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the proceedings are for the recovery of compensation referred to in subsection (3)(b)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings for the recovery of any compensation referred to in subsection (3)(b)" -- other proceedings are not covered
    ELSE (IF `the day the proceedings are commenced` GREATER THAN `period: the last day of a period after` `the day of the allotment` 2 Years
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be commenced after the expiration of 2 years from the date of the allotment" -- commenced within the 2 years, so the bar does not apply (periods ruling (a))

§§ `Section 60(1): what a statement in lieu of prospectus must be`

-- (1)(a) must be signed by every person named in it as a director or a proposed director, or by that person's agent authorised in writing.
-- src:6180 | 60.—(1) To comply with the requirements of this Act, a statement
-- src:6181 | in lieu of prospectus lodged by or on behalf of a company —
-- src:6183 | (a) must be signed by every person who is named therein as a
-- src:6184 | director or a proposed director of the company or by the
-- src:6185 | person’s agent authorised in writing;
@ref s 60(1)(a) (src:6180-6185)
GIVEN `the number of persons named in the statement as a director or a proposed director` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those persons who have signed the statement` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those persons for whom an agent authorised in writing has signed the statement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(1)(a) the statement in lieu of prospectus is signed as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (`the number of those persons who have signed the statement` PLUS `the number of those persons for whom an agent authorised in writing has signed the statement`) AT LEAST `the number of persons named in the statement as a director or a proposed director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; a duty not met): "a statement in lieu of prospectus lodged by or on behalf of a company -- (a) must be signed by every person who is named therein as a director or a proposed director of the company or by the person's agent authorised in writing"

-- (1)(b) must, subject to Part 3 of the Sixth Schedule, be in the form of and state the matters specified in Part 1 of that Schedule and set out the reports
-- specified in Part 2. The detail is in sga1-sixth-schedule.l4; the three facts are taken here as facts (the seat layer asks them as they stand; sga1-sixth-schedule.l4 holds the rows and the reports for a person who wants to check them).
-- src:6187 | (b) must, subject to Part 3 of the Sixth Schedule, be in the form
-- src:6188 | of and state the matters specified in Part 1 of that Schedule
-- src:6189 | and set out the reports specified in Part 2 of that Schedule;
-- src:6190 | and
@ref s 60(1)(b) (src:6187-6190)
GIVEN `the statement is in the form of Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement states the matters specified in Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement sets out the reports specified in Part 2 of the Sixth Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(1)(b) the statement in lieu of prospectus is in the form and has the contents the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF    `the statement is in the form of Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule`
      AND `the statement states the matters specified in Part 1 of the Sixth Schedule`
      AND `the statement sets out the reports specified in Part 2 of the Sixth Schedule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; a duty not met): "(b) must, subject to Part 3 of the Sixth Schedule, be in the form of and state the matters specified in Part 1 of that Schedule and set out the reports specified in Part 2 of that Schedule"

-- (1)(c) where the report makers have made, or indicated without giving reasons, adjustments of the kind in paragraph 5 of Part 3 of the Schedule, the statement must
-- carry a written statement signed by those persons setting out the adjustments and giving the reasons. Where the "where" gate is not met nothing is required (fork F-RS2).
-- src:6192 | (c) must, where the persons making any report specified in
-- src:6193 | Part 2 of that Schedule have made therein or have, without
-- src:6194 | giving the reasons, indicated therein any such adjustments
-- src:6195 | as are mentioned in paragraph 5 of Part 3 of that Schedule,
-- src:6196 | have endorsed thereon or attached thereto a written
-- src:6197 | statement signed by those persons setting out the
-- src:6198 | adjustments and giving the reasons therefor.
@ref s 60(1)(c) (src:6192-6198)
GIVEN `the persons making a report specified in Part 2 have made adjustments in it, or have indicated adjustments in it without giving the reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written statement signed by those persons setting out the adjustments and giving the reasons is endorsed on or attached to the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(1)(c) the statement in lieu of prospectus has the written statement of adjustments the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the persons making a report specified in Part 2 have made adjustments in it, or have indicated adjustments in it without giving the reasons`)
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- the paragraph's "where" gate is not met, so it requires nothing and the statement meets it (fork F-RS2)
    ELSE (IF `a written statement signed by those persons setting out the adjustments and giving the reasons is endorsed on or attached to the statement in lieu of prospectus`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; a duty not met): "must, where the persons making any report specified in Part 2 of that Schedule have made therein or have, without giving the reasons, indicated therein any such adjustments as are mentioned in paragraph 5 of Part 3 of that Schedule, have endorsed thereon or attached thereto a written statement signed by those persons setting out the adjustments and giving the reasons therefor"

-- (1) as a whole: the three requirements together.
-- src:6180 | 60.—(1) To comply with the requirements of this Act, a statement
-- src:6181 | in lieu of prospectus lodged by or on behalf of a company —
@ref s 60(1) (src:6180-6181)
GIVEN `the statement is signed as paragraph (a) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement is in the form and has the contents paragraph (b) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the statement has the written statement of adjustments paragraph (c) requires` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(1) the statement in lieu of prospectus meets the three requirements of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF    (`the statement is signed as paragraph (a) requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND (`the statement is in the form and has the contents paragraph (b) requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
      AND (`the statement has the written statement of adjustments paragraph (c) requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (IF    (`the statement is signed as paragraph (a) requires` EQUALS NOTHING)
             OR (`the statement is in the form and has the contents paragraph (b) requires` EQUALS NOTHING)
             OR (`the statement has the written statement of adjustments paragraph (c) requires` EQUALS NOTHING)
          THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a paragraph the caller could not answer leaves the whole requirement unanswered
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; a duty not met): "To comply with the requirements of this Act, a statement in lieu of prospectus lodged by or on behalf of a company -- (a) must be signed ...; (b) must ...; and (c) must ..."

§§ `Section 60(2): the Registrar must not accept a statement that does not appear to comply`

-- (2) The Registrar must not accept for registration any statement in lieu of prospectus unless it appears to the Registrar to comply with the requirements of this Act.
-- src:6200 | (2) The Registrar must not accept for registration any statement in
-- src:6201 | lieu of prospectus unless it appears to the Registrar to comply with the
-- src:6202 | requirements of this Act.
@ref s 60(2) (src:6200-6202)
GIVEN `it appears to the Registrar that the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(2) the Registrar is barred from accepting the statement in lieu of prospectus for registration` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Registrar that the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not accept for registration any statement in lieu of prospectus unless it appears to the Registrar to comply with the requirements of this Act"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `Section 60(3): an untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure`

-- (3) Where in a statement in lieu of prospectus there is any untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure, a director who signed it is guilty of an offence unless he or she proves
-- that the untrue statement or non-disclosure was immaterial, or that he or she had reasonable ground to believe and, up to the time of delivery for registration, did believe that the
-- untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial. Fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months or both.
-- "Untrue": s 4(3) deems a statement in a statement in lieu of prospectus untrue if misleading in the form and context in which it is included; the statement may also be untrue in fact.
-- src:6204 | (3) Where in any statement in lieu of prospectus there is any untrue
-- src:6205 | statement or wilful non‑disclosure, any director who signed the
-- src:6206 | statement in lieu of prospectus shall, unless he or she proves either
-- src:6207 | that the untrue statement or non‑disclosure was immaterial or that he
-- src:6212 | or she had reasonable ground to believe and did up to the time of the
-- src:6213 | delivery for registration of the statement in lieu of prospectus believe
-- src:6214 | that the untrue statement was true or the non‑disclosure immaterial,
-- src:6215 | be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:6216 | exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- src:6217 | 12 months or to both.
@ref s 60(3) (src:6204-6217)
GIVEN `a statement in the statement in lieu of prospectus is untrue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement in question is misleading in the form and context in which it is included` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(3) the statement in lieu of prospectus contains an untrue statement` MEANS
    IF    `a statement in the statement in lieu of prospectus is untrue`
       OR (`s 4(3) the statement is deemed to be untrue` TRUE `the statement in question is misleading in the form and context in which it is included` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any statement in lieu of prospectus there is any untrue statement" -- a failed "where" (marginal reading (a)); s 4(3) deems a misleading statement untrue and does not say that no other statement is

@ref s 60(3) (src:6204-6217)
GIVEN `the director proves that the untrue statement or non-disclosure was immaterial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director proves that the director had reasonable ground to believe that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director did believe, up to the time of the delivery for registration of the statement in lieu of prospectus, that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(3) the section gives the director a defence on these facts` MEANS
    IF    `the director proves that the untrue statement or non-disclosure was immaterial`
       OR (    `the director proves that the director had reasonable ground to believe that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial`
           AND `the director did believe, up to the time of the delivery for registration of the statement in lieu of prospectus, that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he or she proves either that the untrue statement or non-disclosure was immaterial or that he or she had reasonable ground to believe and did up to the time of the delivery for registration of the statement in lieu of prospectus believe that the untrue statement was true or the non-disclosure immaterial" -- this section gives no defence on these facts (delegated-definitions ruling of 2026-11-05, (b)); it does not say there is no defence at all

@ref s 60(3) (src:6204-6217)
GIVEN `the person is a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains an untrue statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains a wilful non-disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section gives the director a defence on these facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60(3) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus`
      AND (`the statement in lieu of prospectus contains an untrue statement` OR `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains a wilful non-disclosure`)
    THEN (IF `the section gives the director a defence on these facts`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless he or she proves either that the untrue statement or non-disclosure was immaterial or that he or she had reasonable ground to believe ..." -- the defence is made out
          ELSE JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "Where in any statement in lieu of prospectus there is any untrue statement or wilful non-disclosure, any director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus shall ... be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts

@ref s 60(3) (src:6204-6217)
DECLARE `s 60(3) penalty` HAS
    `s 60(3) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 60(3) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 60(3) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 60(3) (src:6204-6217)
GIVEN `the person is a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains an untrue statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains a wilful non-disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the section gives the director a defence on these facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 60(3) penalty`
`s 60(3) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 60(3) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the person is a director who signed the statement in lieu of prospectus` `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains an untrue statement` `the statement in lieu of prospectus contains a wilful non-disclosure` `the section gives the director a defence on these facts` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 60(3) penalty` OF 5000, 12, TRUE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 61: restrictions on commencement of business`

§§ `Section 61(1): a company that has issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe`

-- (1) Where a company having a share capital has issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares, it must not commence any business or exercise any
-- borrowing power (a) if money is or may become liable to be repaid to applicants by reason of any failure to apply for or obtain permission for listing; or (b) unless
-- (i) shares held subject to payment of the whole amount in cash have been allotted to an amount not less than the minimum subscription; (ii) every director has paid the
-- proportion payable on application and allotment on each of the shares he or she took, for which he or she is liable to pay in cash; and (iii) a declaration in the prescribed form
-- verifying (i) and (ii) has been lodged with the Registrar by the secretary or one of the directors, or by a registered qualified individual authorised by the company.
-- The "Where" gate: when it fails the bar does not apply (periods ruling (b)): JUST FALSE. The "minimum subscription" is the keel's s 4(1) term.
-- src:6222 | 61.—(1) Where a company having a share capital has issued a
-- src:6223 | prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares, the company
-- src:6224 | must not commence any business or exercise any borrowing
-- src:6225 | power —
-- src:6227 | (a) if any money is or may become liable to be repaid to
-- src:6228 | applicants for any shares or debentures offered for public
-- src:6229 | subscription by reason of any failure to apply for or obtain
-- src:6230 | permission for listing for quotation on any securities
-- src:6231 | exchange; or
-- src:6233 | (b) unless —
-- src:6235 | (i) shares held subject to the payment of the whole
-- src:6236 | amount thereof in cash have been allotted to an
-- src:6237 | amount not less in the whole than the minimum
-- src:6238 | subscription;
-- src:6240 | (ii) every director has paid to the company on each of the
-- src:6241 | shares taken or contracted to be taken by him or her,
-- src:6242 | and for which he or she is liable to pay in cash, a
-- src:6243 | proportion equal to the proportion payable on
-- src:6244 | application and allotment on the shares offered for
-- src:6245 | public subscription; and
-- src:6247 | (iii) there has been lodged with the Registrar a
-- src:6248 | declaration in the prescribed form by —
-- src:6250 | (A) the secretary or one of the directors of the
-- src:6251 | company; or
-- src:6253 | (B) a registered qualified individual authorised by
-- src:6254 | the company,
-- src:6259 | (iii) verifying that sub‑paragraphs (i) and (ii) have been
-- src:6260 | complied with.
@ref s 61(1) (src:6222-6260)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `money is or may become liable to be repaid to applicants for shares or debentures offered for public subscription by reason of a failure to apply for or obtain permission for listing for quotation on a securities exchange` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the shares held subject to the payment of the whole amount thereof in cash that have been allotted, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum amount which the prospectus states must be raised by the issue of the shares offered, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `every director has paid to the company on each share taken or contracted to be taken, for which the director is liable to pay in cash, a proportion equal to the proportion payable on application and allotment on the shares offered for public subscription` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that sub-paragraphs (i) and (ii) have been complied with has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration was made by the secretary or one of the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration was made by a registered qualified individual authorised by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(1) the company is barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company has a share capital` AND `the company has issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a company having a share capital has issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares, the company must not commence any business or exercise any borrowing power" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b)); marginal reading (a)
    ELSE (IF `money is or may become liable to be repaid to applicants for shares or debentures offered for public subscription by reason of a failure to apply for or obtain permission for listing for quotation on a securities exchange`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE (IF    `s 61(1)(b)(i) the amount allotted is not less than the minimum subscription` `the amount of the shares held subject to the payment of the whole amount thereof in cash that have been allotted, in Singapore dollars` `the minimum amount which the prospectus states must be raised by the issue of the shares offered, in Singapore dollars`
                    AND `every director has paid to the company on each share taken or contracted to be taken, for which the director is liable to pay in cash, a proportion equal to the proportion payable on application and allotment on the shares offered for public subscription`
                    AND `a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that sub-paragraphs (i) and (ii) have been complied with has been lodged with the Registrar`
                    AND (`the declaration was made by the secretary or one of the directors of the company` OR `the declaration was made by a registered qualified individual authorised by the company`)
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) unless -- (i) shares held subject to the payment of the whole amount thereof in cash have been allotted to an amount not less in the whole than the minimum subscription; (ii) every director has paid ...; and (iii) there has been lodged with the Registrar a declaration in the prescribed form" -- every condition of the "unless" is met
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

-- (1)(b)(i) alone: "shares held subject to the payment of the whole amount thereof in cash have been allotted to an amount not less in the whole than the minimum subscription".
-- The minimum subscription is s 4(1) "minimum subscription" (the amount the prospectus states as the minimum the directors think must be raised).
@ref s 61(1)(b)(i) (src:6235-6238)
GIVEN `the amount of the shares held subject to the payment of the whole amount thereof in cash that have been allotted, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum amount which the prospectus states must be raised by the issue of the shares offered, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 61(1)(b)(i) the amount allotted is not less than the minimum subscription` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(1) "minimum subscription" the minimum subscription` TRUE `the minimum amount which the prospectus states must be raised by the issue of the shares offered, in Singapore dollars`
    WHEN JUST minimum THEN `the amount of the shares held subject to the payment of the whole amount thereof in cash that have been allotted, in Singapore dollars` AT LEAST minimum
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

DECLARE `s 61 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 61(1) commence business or exercise a borrowing power before the conditions of paragraph (b) are met`
    `s 61(2) commence business or exercise a borrowing power before the conditions of paragraph (a) to (c) are met`

@ref s 61(1) (src:6222-6260)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 61 act`
`s 61(1) a company that issued a prospectus must not commence business before the conditions are met` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 61(1) commence business or exercise a borrowing power before the conditions of paragraph (b) are met`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company commenced business or exercised a borrowing power before the conditions of section 61(1)(b) were met"

§§ `Section 61(2): a public company that has not issued a prospectus`

-- (2) Where a public company having a share capital has not issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares, it must not commence any business or exercise any
-- borrowing power unless (a) a complying statement in lieu of prospectus has been lodged with the Registrar; (b) every director has paid the proportion payable on application and
-- allotment on each share taken, for which he or she is liable to pay in cash; and (c) a declaration in the prescribed form verifying paragraph (b) has been lodged with the Registrar by
-- the secretary or one of the directors, or by a registered qualified individual authorised by the company.
-- src:6264 | (2) Where a public company having a share capital has not issued a
-- src:6265 | prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares, the company
-- src:6266 | must not commence any business or exercise any borrowing power
-- src:6267 | unless —
-- src:6269 | (a) there has been lodged with the Registrar a statement in lieu
-- src:6270 | of prospectus which complies with the provisions of this
-- src:6271 | Act;
-- src:6273 | (b) every director of the company has paid to the company on
-- src:6274 | each of the shares taken or contracted to be taken by him or
-- src:6275 | her, and for which he or she is liable to pay in cash, a
-- src:6276 | proportion equal to the proportion payable on application
-- src:6277 | and allotment on the shares payable in cash; and
-- src:6279 | (c) there has been lodged with the Registrar a declaration in
-- src:6280 | the prescribed form by —
-- src:6282 | (i) the secretary or one of the directors of the company;
-- src:6283 | or
-- src:6285 | (ii) a registered qualified individual authorised by the
-- src:6286 | company,
-- src:6288 | (c) verifying that paragraph (b) has been complied with.
@ref s 61(2) (src:6264-6288)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement in lieu of prospectus has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every director has paid to the company on each share taken or contracted to be taken, for which the director is liable to pay in cash, a proportion equal to the proportion payable on application and allotment on the shares payable in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that paragraph (b) has been complied with has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration was made by the secretary or one of the directors of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration was made by a registered qualified individual authorised by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(2) the company is barred from commencing business or exercising a borrowing power` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is a public company` AND `the company has a share capital` AND (NOT `the company has issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a public company having a share capital has not issued a prospectus inviting the public to subscribe for its shares, the company must not commence any business or exercise any borrowing power" -- a failed "where" (periods ruling (b)); marginal reading (a)
    ELSE (IF    `a statement in lieu of prospectus has been lodged with the Registrar`
            AND `the statement in lieu of prospectus complies with the requirements of this Act`
            AND `every director has paid to the company on each share taken or contracted to be taken, for which the director is liable to pay in cash, a proportion equal to the proportion payable on application and allotment on the shares payable in cash`
            AND `a declaration in the prescribed form verifying that paragraph (b) has been complied with has been lodged with the Registrar`
            AND (`the declaration was made by the secretary or one of the directors of the company` OR `the declaration was made by a registered qualified individual authorised by the company`)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not commence any business or exercise any borrowing power unless -- (a) there has been lodged with the Registrar a statement in lieu of prospectus which complies with the provisions of this Act; (b) every director of the company has paid ...; and (c) there has been lodged with the Registrar a declaration in the prescribed form" -- every condition of the "unless" is met
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 61(2) (src:6264-6288)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 61 act`
`s 61(2) a public company without a prospectus must not commence business before the conditions are met` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    SHANT `s 61(2) commence business or exercise a borrowing power before the conditions of paragraph (a) to (c) are met`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company commenced business or exercised a borrowing power before the conditions of section 61(2) were met"

§§ `Section 61(3): the Registrar's notice`

-- (3) The Registrar must, on lodgment of the declaration under (1)(b)(iii) or (2)(c), issue a notice in the prescribed form that the company is entitled to commence business and to
-- exercise its borrowing powers; and that notice is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in it.
-- A duty on an official: what it means for the company is that the notice follows the lodgment. "on lodgment": a gate that counts as "where" (delegated-definitions ruling (c)); a duty whose gate is unmet
-- answers JUST FALSE here (the Registrar is not obliged yet), a case-by-case site (fork line F-RS3).
-- src:6292 | (3) The Registrar must, on the lodgment of the declaration under
-- src:6293 | subsection (1)(b)(iii) or (2)(c) (as the case may be), issue a notice in
-- src:6294 | the prescribed form that the company is entitled to commence
-- src:6295 | business and to exercise its borrowing powers; and that notice is
-- src:6296 | conclusive evidence of the matters stated in it.
@ref s 61(3) (src:6292-6296)
GIVEN `a declaration under subsection (1)(b)(iii) or (2)(c) has been lodged with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(3) the Registrar must issue the notice that the company is entitled to commence business` MEANS
    IF `a declaration under subsection (1)(b)(iii) or (2)(c) has been lodged with the Registrar`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must, on the lodgment of the declaration under subsection (1)(b)(iii) or (2)(c) (as the case may be), issue a notice" -- no declaration is lodged, so the duty has not arisen (a duty whose "on the lodgment of the declaration" gate is unmet: fork line F-RS3)

@ref s 61(3) (src:6292-6296)
GIVEN `the Registrar has issued the notice under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(3) the notice is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in it` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has issued the notice under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that notice is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in it" -- says nothing of any other document

§§ `Section 61(4): a contract made before the company may commence business`

-- (4) Any contract made by a company before the date on which it is entitled to commence business is provisional only and is not binding on the company until that date,
-- and on that date it becomes binding. The "until" bar (delegated-definitions ruling (d)): JUST TRUE before the date, JUST FALSE from it.
-- src:6298 | (4) Any contract made by a company before the date on which it is
-- src:6299 | entitled to commence business is provisional only and is not binding
-- src:6300 | on the company until that date, and on that date it becomes binding.
@ref s 61(4) (src:6298-6300)
GIVEN `the contract was made by the company before the date on which it is entitled to commence business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the company is entitled to commence business` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(4) the contract is provisional only and not yet binding on the company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the contract was made by the company before the date on which it is entitled to commence business`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any contract made by a company before the date on which it is entitled to commence business" -- a contract made on or after that date is not covered
    ELSE (IF `the day on which the question is asked` LESS THAN `the date on which the company is entitled to commence business`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not binding on the company until that date, and on that date it becomes binding" -- the date has come, so the contract is no longer only provisional

§§ `Section 61(5): money payable on application for the debentures`

-- (5) Where shares and debentures are offered simultaneously by a company for subscription, nothing in this section prevents the receipt by the company of any money payable on
-- application for the debentures.
-- src:6302 | (5) Where shares and debentures are offered simultaneously by a
-- src:6303 | company for subscription, nothing in this section prevents the receipt
-- src:6304 | by the company of any money payable on application for the
-- src:6305 | debentures.
@ref s 61(5) (src:6302-6305)
GIVEN `shares and debentures are offered simultaneously by the company for subscription` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money is payable on application for the debentures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(5) section 61 prevents the company from receiving the money` MEANS
    IF `shares and debentures are offered simultaneously by the company for subscription` AND `the money is payable on application for the debentures`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this section prevents the receipt by the company of any money payable on application for the debentures"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative covers only money payable on application for debentures offered together with shares; it says nothing of other money

§§ `Section 61(6): the offence of commencing business in contravention`

-- (6) If any company commences business or exercises borrowing powers in contravention of this section, every person who is responsible for the contravention is guilty of an
-- offence: a fine not exceeding $4,000 and a default penalty of $250.
-- src:6310 | (6) If any company commences business or exercises borrowing
-- src:6311 | powers in contravention of this section, every person who is
-- src:6312 | responsible for the contravention shall be guilty of an offence and
-- src:6313 | shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $4,000 and to a
-- src:6314 | default penalty of $250.
@ref s 61(6) (src:6310-6314)
DECLARE `s 61(6) penalty` HAS
    `s 61(6) the highest fine, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `s 61(6) the longest imprisonment, in months` IS A NUMBER
    `s 61(6) the court may impose both the fine and the imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 61(6) a default penalty is also payable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 61(6) the default penalty, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
@ref s 61(6) (src:6310-6314)
GIVEN `the company commenced business or exercised borrowing powers in contravention of section 61` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is responsible for the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF    `the company commenced business or exercised borrowing powers in contravention of section 61`
      AND `the person is responsible for the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), fork line in NOTES.md): "If any company commences business or exercises borrowing powers in contravention of this section, every person who is responsible for the contravention shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet, so this subsection makes the person guilty of nothing on these facts; it does not say the person is innocent of any other offence
@ref s 61(6) (src:6310-6314)
GIVEN `the company commenced business or exercised borrowing powers in contravention of section 61` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is responsible for the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 61(6) penalty`
`s 61(6) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 61(6) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `the company commenced business or exercised borrowing powers in contravention of section 61` `the person is responsible for the contravention` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (`s 61(6) penalty` OF 4000, 0, FALSE, TRUE, 250)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty


§§ `Section 61(7): the Registrar's certificate`

-- (7) Upon the application of a company which has received a notice under (3) and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue a certificate confirming that the company is
-- entitled to commence business and to exercise its borrowing powers, and that certificate is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in it.
-- src:6316 | (7) Upon the application of a company which has received a notice
-- src:6317 | under subsection (3) and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar
-- src:6318 | must issue to the company a certificate confirming that the company
-- src:6319 | is entitled to commence business and to exercise its borrowing
-- src:6320 | powers, and that certificate is conclusive evidence of the matters
-- src:6321 | stated in it.
@ref s 61(7) (src:6316-6321)
GIVEN `the company has received a notice under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has applied for the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(7) the Registrar must issue the certificate that the company is entitled to commence business` MEANS
    IF    `the company has received a notice under subsection (3)`
      AND `the company has applied for the certificate`
      AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of a company which has received a notice under subsection (3) and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the company a certificate" -- an "upon" gate that is unmet (delegated-definitions ruling (c): "upon" counts as "where"); the duty has not arisen (fork line F-RS3)

@ref s 61(7) (src:6316-6321)
GIVEN `the Registrar has issued the certificate under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 61(7) the certificate is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in it` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar has issued the certificate under subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that certificate is conclusive evidence of the matters stated in it" -- says nothing of any other document

§ `Section 62: restriction on varying contracts referred to in the prospectus`

-- 62. A company must not before the statutory meeting vary the terms of a contract referred to in the prospectus or statement in lieu of prospectus, unless the variation is made
-- subject to the approval of the statutory meeting.
-- src:6325 | 62. A company must not before the statutory meeting vary the
-- src:6326 | terms of a contract referred to in the prospectus or statement in lieu of
-- src:6327 | prospectus, unless the variation is made subject to the approval of the
-- src:6328 | statutory meeting.
@ref s 62 (src:6325-6328)
GIVEN `the contract is referred to in the prospectus or the statement in lieu of prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation is made before the statutory meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation is made subject to the approval of the statutory meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62 the company is barred from varying the terms of the contract` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the contract is referred to in the prospectus or the statement in lieu of prospectus`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a contract referred to in the prospectus or statement in lieu of prospectus" -- another contract is not covered
    ELSE (IF (NOT `the variation is made before the statutory meeting`)
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not before the statutory meeting vary the terms" -- the variation is not made before the statutory meeting (a period the text fixes in its own words: periods ruling (a))
          ELSE (IF `the variation is made subject to the approval of the statutory meeting`
                THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the variation is made subject to the approval of the statutory meeting"
                ELSE JUST TRUE))

DECLARE `s 62 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 62 vary the terms of a contract referred to in the prospectus before the statutory meeting without making the variation subject to its approval`

